a Workgroup_reduce or Grid Retype of a loop inside the scope a materializing Unroll minted around a privatized tile's update is refused at the Retype, typed, naming the hardware loop in the scope: true
a Stage whose anchor that scope binds is refused at the Stage, typed, naming the anchor bound inside the scope: true
the same three schedules without Privatize are refused the same way: the rule is the scope's: true
op_legality asked of the program the Privatize and the Unroll left calls all three ops illegal, with the refusal apply raises, and probing the Stage leaves that program's traced store as it was: true
a Vectorized retype or an in-place Unroll of that scope-nested loop, and the same Stage applied ahead of the Unroll (its loads then keep the nest from minting a scope), are admitted by apply and not called illegal by op_legality: true
without a breaking op the privatized tile stays f32, passes the re-check, and executes to the entry program's once-narrowed value (258): true
after a Privatize, a Grid or Workgroup Retype of a loop the tile's cell omits, between the tile's transfers and its update, is refused at the Retype, typed, through apply_classified and schedule_legality: true
op_legality judging that Retype alone, on the program an earlier apply privatized, does not call it illegal: it has no record of the tile: true
on a storage-precision tile, a Grid Retype of an inner loop its cell mentions, or of the privatized loop itself, is refused at the Retype too: true
a Grid Retype of a loop enclosing the tile's transfers, and a Vectorized Retype of the omitted loop, are admitted: true
a Privatize over the outer half of a Split of the localizing loop widens like that loop (258 with the serial rendering, on an f32 tile): true
a Privatize over the inner half of that Split keeps a bf16 storage tile and the split schedule's own narrowing (256, as without Privatize): true
a Privatize over the outer half of a Split of a loop inside the localizing level keeps a bf16 storage tile and the schedule's own narrowing (256, as without Privatize): true
a Privatize over the loop a Coalesce merged from the localizing loop and the loop inside it, and one over the outer half of a Split of that merged loop, widen like the localizing loop (258 with the serial rendering, on an f32 tile): true
a Privatize over the inner half of that Split of the merged loop keeps a bf16 storage tile and the split schedule's own narrowing (256, as without Privatize): true
a Privatize over a segment of a Partition of the localizing loop keeps a bf16 storage tile and the partitioned schedule's own narrowing (256, as without Privatize): true
the program the Split_reduce legs schedule localizes the node accumulated beside the Split_reduce target at its own inner loop, widened there: true
a Privatize of that node over a Split_reduce's block loop, or over its in-block loop, keeps a bf16 storage tile and the split schedule's own narrowing (256, as without Privatize): true
